# 20261005T013747-1001-192-168-30-104-26668.wav
#
# A 14400 call modec placed through the bench, with one RTP packet lost
# in the middle of it: 20 ms of exact zeros at 23.34 s, five seconds
# before the reference sends its eight lines.
#
# The first fixture with a .sent beside it -- what modec transmitted on
# the call, lined up with what it received -- because nothing about
# this call can be replayed without it.  Our own echo is on this line
# half a second late and 18 dB under the far end, and a replay that
# regenerates its transmit has no reference to cancel it with.
#
# What the lost packet did: for those 20 ms the line held nothing but
# the canceller's prediction of the echo, subtracted from zeros -- a
# clean V.32 signal twenty decibels down -- and the equaliser, whose
# step is divided by the power in its window, trained on it.  The line
# was the same line afterwards; the equaliser was not, the receiver
# read 18 dB where it had read 30, and one line of the eight arrived.
# Held through the hole ('Modec.QAM.qrFadeHold'), all eight do.
#
# The bytes before the first line are what the hole itself decodes to,
# which is why this one has a tolerance; the lines are what must not
# move.
seconds:   36.0
role:      originate
modes:     v32bis
v8:        no
connect:   V32bis 14400
retrains:  0
expect:    B0000 pack my box with five dozen liquor jugs 9876543210
expect:    B0001 pack my box with five dozen liquor jugs 9876543210
expect:    B0002 pack my box with five dozen liquor jugs 9876543210
expect:    B0003 pack my box with five dozen liquor jugs 9876543210
expect:    B0004 pack my box with five dozen liquor jugs 9876543210
expect:    B0005 pack my box with five dozen liquor jugs 9876543210
expect:    B0006 pack my box with five dozen liquor jugs 9876543210
expect:    B0007 pack my box with five dozen liquor jugs 9876543210
tolerance: 24
